course: dictionary
lesson: 3709
title: Fleet: a group that sails or travels together
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around it, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «In 1788 the First Fleet of eleven ships brought British convicts and soldiers to Sydney Cove.» The word eleven and the word ships are clues: a fleet is a group of ships that sail together.
explain: «Long before Europeans arrived, the Indian Ocean was a busy sea of trade, with huge Chinese fleets under Zheng He.» Busy, trade and sea are clues. A fleet here is a big group of ships. Try it: swap in the word group of ships, and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Fleet can also be a group of vehicles owned by one company, like a fleet of taxis or vans. The word fleet also has a rare meaning: fleet of foot means quick and light on your feet. Look at the words around it, and you will know which meaning is right.
fact: A fleet is a group of ships, or of vehicles, that travel together.
fact: A fleet of ships is often called a navy fleet when it belongs to a country's navy.
fact: A fishing fleet is a group of fishing boats that sail from the same port.
fact: «The First Fleet» was eleven ships that brought convicts and soldiers to Sydney Cove in 1788.
fact: «Fleet-footed» means quick and light on your feet, and it is a literary word you will meet in stories and poems.
exercise: «In 1788 the First Fleet of eleven ships brought convicts and soldiers to Sydney Cove.» How many ships were in the First Fleet? | None | Two | *Eleven | Twenty
exercise: What is a fleet of taxis? | *A group of taxis owned by one company | A map of the city | A road where taxis wait | One taxi with a driver
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Long before Europeans arrived, the Indian Ocean was a busy sea of trade, with great ports like Malacca and Kilwa.» that means a place where ships load and unload. | busy | sea | trade | *ports
exercise: «She was fleet of foot and won the race.» What does fleet of foot mean? | Good at swimming | Afraid of running | Slow and heavy | *Quick and light on her feet
test: «Huge Chinese fleets under Zheng He sailed across the Indian Ocean.» What does fleets mean here? | Gardens full of flowers | Markets selling food | *Groups of ships sailing together | Single large boats
test: A fishing fleet is | A lake full of fish | *A group of fishing boats that sail together | A net for catching fish | A fish shop by the harbour
exam: In which phrase does fleet mean quick and light on your feet? | A fleet of ships | *Fleet of foot | A fishing fleet | A fleet of vans
